A||||1||maryjane||Birthday greetings- & a little bragging||||1||
Z||000000||maryjane||11-10-2001||01:45 AM||||Yesterday, WampusCat wrote in the Veterans/Remembrance Day thread-"225.997 and counting." He knew what I was talking about in that thread, he's a Marine too.<BR>It's now November 10th. My birthday, and a lot of other's. Ask any Marine when they were born and they will all tell you Nov 10, 1775. We're 226 years old. We may forget wives & GF's birthdays/anniversaries, but not this date. A few things about Marines:<P>ONCE A MARINE-ALWAYS A MARINE<BR>There are no ex-Marines or former Marines. There are retired Marines, Marine reservists, active-duty Marines, and Marine veterans. Nonetheless, once one has EARNED the title, he remains a Marine for life. <P>First To Fight- Started in WWI. US Marines were the first American fighting unit to engage the Germans. They've been at or near  the forefront of every military engagment ever since. I quote from a India news service report dated Sept 15,2001:<BR>"Another daily, The News, quoted an eyewitness as saying that he had seen a small contingent of U.S. troops having already landed in Islamabad. It is said, according to unofficial reports, a contingent of over 50 personnel from the Special Services Group of the US Marines 'Green Seals" have landed for conducting 'target oriented' operations against bin Laden, prime suspect in the terrorist strikes in the Us."<BR>Marine Quotations: (No offense intended to any other branch of the military, I didn't write em, just quoting them <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>"The safest place in Korea was right behind a platoon of Marines. Lord, how they could fight!"[MGEN Frank Lowe, US Army Korea,1950]<BR>"Why in the hell can't the Army do it if the Marines can? They are the same kind of men, why can't they be like Marines?"[Gen Blackjack Pershing, US Army, 12 Feb 1918]<BR>"We have two companies of Marines running rampant all over the nrthern half of this island and three Army regiments pinned down in the SW corner, doing nothing! What the He** is going on?"[Gen J.W. Vessy Jr.,Us Army, Chairman of the Joint Chiefs of Staff; during the assualt on Grenada,1983]<BR>"Some people spend a lifetime wondering if they made a difference in the world. But, the Marines don't have that problem.[Ronald Reagan,US President;1985]<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/RG181sforgive.jpg"> <BR>Happy Birthday, Marines. <BR>Semper Fi. Good night Chesty, where ever you are.<BR>Don||||reg||1
Z||000001||WampusCat||11-10-2001||09:36 AM||||"Among the men who fought on Iwo Jima, uncommon valor was a common virtue." <P>(Fleet Admiral Chester W. Nimitz, USN, 16 March 1945.) <P>"I have just returned from visiting the Marines at the front, and there is not a finer fighting organization in the world." <P>(General Douglas MacArthur, USA, outskirts of Seoul, 21 September 1950.) <P>"I can't say enough about the two Marine divisions. If I use words like brilliant, it would really be an under-description of the absolutely superb job they did in breaching the so-called impenetrable barrier. . .Absolutely superb operation, a textbook, and I think it'll be studied for many, many years to come as the way to do it." <P>(General H. Norman Schwarzkopf, USA, Riyadh, Saudi Arabia, 27 February 1991.) <P>Happy birthday Devil Dogs!! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/MOLlogo-2.gif"> ||||reg||1
